            %p
          %p
            This is sometimes also known as the morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
            being ‘’weakly orthogonal to’‘ the morphism
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
            are as above, the diagonal morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi h
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h
            exists and is also required to be unique.
          %p
          #LiftingForObjects.num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              %strong (lifting properties of objects)
              %br/
              One also speaks of
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
              having left or right lifting properties (for instance in the definition of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+objects"} projective objects
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injective+objects"} injective objects
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrant+objects"} cofibrant objects
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibrant+objects"} fibrant objects
          %ul
            %li
              that the corresponding unique morphisms
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∅
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \varnothing \longrightarrow B
              (from the
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+object"} initial object
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LiftingPropertiesOfMorphisms"}
              (against the given morphism
              = succeed "):" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
