          %p
          #QuillenNegation.num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal+class"}> orthogonal class
                \/
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+negation"}> Quillen negation
                )
              %br/
              Given a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/class"} class
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi Mor
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M \;\subset\; Mor(\mathcal{C})
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
              in a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            %ul
              %li
                %em left weak orthogonal class
                or
                %em
                  left
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+negation"} Quillen negation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mmultiscripts
                        %mi M
                        %mprescripts
                        %none
                        %mi ⧄
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \multiscripts{^&amp;solb;}{M}{}
            %p or
            %ul
              %li
                %em right weak orthogonal class
                or
                %em
                  right
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+negation"} Quillen negation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mmultiscripts
                        %mi M
                        %none
                        %mi ⧄
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \multiscripts{}{M}{^&amp;solb;}
            %p
              is the class of all morphisms which have the left, respectively right, lifting property (in the sense of Def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LiftingPropertiesOfMorphisms"}
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi M
                      %mi ⧄
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} {
                    %mi p
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ∈
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi Mor
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} |
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %munder
                      %mo ∀
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi M
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi i
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi ⧄
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} }
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mrow
                      %mi ⧄
                    %mi M
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} {
                    %mi i
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ∈
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi Mor
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} |
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %munder
                      %mo ∀
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi M
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi i
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi ⧄
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} }
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    M^{&amp;solb;}
                    \\;\coloneqq\;
                    \\Big\{
                    p \,\in\, Mor(\mathcal{C})
                    \\;\big\vert\;
                    \\underset{i \in M}{\forall}
                    \\; i \,&amp;solb;\, p
                    \\Big\},
                    \\;\;\;\;\;
                    {}^{&amp;solb;}M
                    \\;\coloneqq\;
                    \\Big\{
                    i \,\in\, Mor(\mathcal{C})
                    \\;\big\vert\;
                    \\underset{p \in M}{\forall}
                    \\; i \,&amp;solb;\, p
                    \\Big\}
                    \\,.
            %p
          %h2#ExamplesOfLiftingProperties Examples of lifting properties
          %p Decyphering notation in most of the examples below leads to standard definitions or reformulations. The intuition behind most examples below is that the class of morphisms consists of simple or archetypal examples related to the property defined.
          %p
            We use the notation of Def.
            = succeed "." do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#QuillenNegation"}
          %h3#elementary_examples Elementary examples
          %h4#sets Sets
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} {
                      %mo ∅
                      %mo →
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %msup
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} }
                        %mi ⧄
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo =
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi Srjctv
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\big\{
                      \\varnothing \to \{*\}\big
                      \\}^{&amp;solb;}
                      \\;\;\;
                      \=
                      \\;\;\;
                      Srjctv
              %p
                is the class of
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/surjective+functions"} surjective functions
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mi a
                      %mo ,
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mo →
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %msup
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                        %mi ⧄
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo =
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi Injctv
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\big( \{a,b\}\to \{*\} \big)^{&amp;solb;}
                      \\;\;\;
                      \=
                      \\;\;\;
                      Injctv
              %p
                is the class of
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injective+functions"} injective functions
          %h4#ExamplesModules Modules
          %p
            In the category
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/RMod"} RMod
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module"} modules
            over a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+ring"} commutative ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            (recalling that we use thenotation of Def.
            = succeed "):" do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#QuillenNegation"}
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/surjection"} surjective
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphisms"} homomorphisms
            are those with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+lifting+property"} right lifting property
            against the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+object"} initial
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
            from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zero"} zero
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module"} module
            into the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ground+ring"} ground ring
          #eq:SurjectiveModuleMapsAsRightOrthClass.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mn 0
                  %mo →
                  %mi R
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mi ⧄
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi Srjctv
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\{ 0 \to R \}^{&amp;solb;}
                  \\;\;\;=\;\;\;
                  Srjctv
                  \\,.
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injection"} injective
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphisms"} homomorphisms
            are those with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+lifting+property"} right lifting property
            against the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
            from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ground+ring"} ground ring
            into the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zero"} zero
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module"} module
          #eq:InjectiveModuleMapsAsRightOrthClass.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (2)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi R
                  %mo →
                  %mn 0
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mi ⧄
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi Injctv
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\{ R \to 0 \}^{&amp;solb;}
                  \\;\;\;=\;\;\;
                  Injctv
                  \\,.
          %p
            An
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module"} module
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+module"} projective
            iff (by direct unwinding of the definitions of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+objects"} projective objects
            and lifts) the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+object"} initial morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                  %mo →
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \to R
            (out of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zero"} zero
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module"} module
            into the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ground+ring"} ground ring
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+lifting+property"} left lifting property
            against all surjective homomorphisms.
          %p
            With the notation of Def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#QuillenNegation"}
            this reads as follows:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mtext projective
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ⇔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
