                        %mi p
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
          %h3#in_algebraic_topology_and_in_model_categories In algebraic topology and in model categories
          %p
            Lifting properties are paramount in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+topology"} algebraic topology
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+categories"} model categories
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+factorization+systems"} weak factorization systems
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrations"} cofibrations
                in a model category are precisely the class with the left lifting property against the
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/acyclic+fibrations"} acyclic fibrations
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibrations"} fibrations
                in a model category are precisely the class with the right lifting property against the
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/acyclic+cofibrations"} acyclic cofibrations
          %h4#serre_fibrations_of_topological_spaces Serre fibrations of topological spaces
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+topological+spaces"} classical model structure on topological spaces
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Top
                    %mi Qu
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top_{Qu}
            is controlled by the following lifting properties:
          %p
            consider let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_0
            be the class of maps
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mi n
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi D
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^n\to D^{n+1}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/embeddings"} embeddings
            of the boundary
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mi n
                  %mo =
                  %mo ∂
                  %msup
                    %mi D
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^n=\partial D^{n+1}
            of a ball into the ball
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi D
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D^{n+1}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi WC
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} WC_0
            be the class of maps embedding the upper semi-sphere into the disk.
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi WC
                    %mn 0
                    %mrow
                      %mi ⧄
                      %mi ℓ
                  %mo ,
                  %msubsup
                    %mi WC
                    %mn 0
                    %mrow
                      %mi ⧄
                      %mi ℓ
                      %mi r
                  %mo ,
                  %msubsup
                    %mi C
                    %mn 0
                    %mrow
                      %mi ⧄
                      %mi ℓ
                  %mo ,
                  %msubsup
                    %mi C
                    %mn 0
                    %mrow
                      %mi ⧄
                      %mi ℓ
                      %mi r
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} WC_0^{&amp;solb; \ell}, WC_0^{&amp;solb; \ell r}, C_0^{&amp;solb; \ell}, C_0^{&amp;solb; \ell r}
            are the classes of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Serre+fibrations"} Serre fibrations
            %a{:href => "https://archive.org/details/arxiv-math9803002"} Hovey, Model Categories, Def. 2.4.3, Th.2.4.9
          %h4#hurewicz_fibrations_of_topological_spaces Hurewicz fibrations of topological spaces
          %p
            A map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi U
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:U\to B
            has the ‘’path lifting property’‘ iff
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi ⧄
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{0\}\to [0,1] \,\,&amp;solb;\,\, f
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{0\} \to [0,1]
            is the inclusion of one end point of the closed interval into the interval
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [0,1]
          %p
            A map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi U
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:U\to B
            has the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+lifting+property"} homotopy lifting property
            iff
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                  %mo ×
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi ⧄
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to X\times [0,1] \,\,&amp;solb;\,\, f
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                  %mo ×
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\to X\times [0,1]
            is the map
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ↦
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \mapsto (x,0)
          %h4#kan_fibrations_of_simplicial_sets Kan fibrations of simplicial sets
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"} classical model structure on simplicial sets
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi sSet
                    %mi Qu
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet_{Qu}
            is controlled by the following lifting properties:
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_0
            be the class of boundary inclusions
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∂
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo →
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \partial \Delta[n] \to \Delta[n]
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi WC
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} WC_0
            be the class of horn inclusions
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Λ
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo →
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda^i[n] \to \Delta[n]
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+fibrations"} Kan fibrations
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi WC
                      %mn 0
                      %mrow
                        %mi ⧄
                        %mi ℓ
                    %mo ,
                    %msubsup
                      %mi WC
                      %mn 0
                      %mrow
                        %mi ⧄
                        %mi ℓ
                        %mi r
                    %mo ,
                    %msubsup
                      %mi C
                      %mn 0
                      %mrow
                        %mi ⧄
                        %mi ℓ
                    %mo ,
                    %msubsup
                      %mi C
                      %mn 0
                      %mrow
                        %mi ⧄
                        %mi ℓ
                        %mi r
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} WC_0^{&amp;solb; \ell}, WC_0^{&amp;solb; \ell r}, C_0^{&amp;solb; \ell}, C_0^{&amp;solb; \ell r}
            %a{:href => "https://archive.org/details/arxiv-math9803002"} (Model Categories, Def. 3.2.1, Th.3.6.5)
          %h4#degreewise_surjections_of_chain_complexes Degreewise surjections of chain complexes
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+chain+complexes"} model structure on chain complexes
            is controlled by the following lifting properties:
          %ul
            %li
              Let
              = succeed "(" do
                %em Ch
              = succeed ")" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complexes"} chain complexes
              over a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+ring"} commutative ring
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_0
              be the class of maps of form
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo →
                    %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %mi R
                    %mo →
                    %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo →
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo →
                    %mi R
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} id
                    %mi R
                    %mo →
                    %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \cdots\to 0\to R \to 0 \to 0 \to \cdots \to \cdots \to R \xrightarrow{\operatorname{id}} R \to 0 \to 0 \to \cdots,
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi WC
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} WC_0
              be
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo →
                    %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo →
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo →
                    %mi R
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} id
                    %mi R
                    %mo →
                    %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \cdots \to 0\to 0 \to 0 \to 0 \to \cdots \to \cdots \to R \xrightarrow{\operatorname{id}} R \to 0 \to 0 \to \cdots.
              Then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi WC
                      %mn 0
