                        %mi ⧄
                        %mi ℓ
                    %mo ,
                    %msubsup
                      %mi C
                      %mn 0
                      %mrow
                        %mi ⧄
                        %mi ℓ
                        %mi r
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} WC_0^{&amp;solb; \ell}, WC_0^{&amp;solb; \ell r}, C_0^{&amp;solb; \ell}, C_0^{&amp;solb; \ell r}
              are the classes of fibrations, acyclic cofibrations, acyclic fibrations, and cofibrations.
              %a{:href => "https://archive.org/details/arxiv-math9803002"} (Model Categories, Def. 2.3.3, Th.2.3.11)
          %h3#topology Topology
          %p
            Many elementary properties in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/general+topology"} general topology
            %em Top
            of topological spaces. This leads to a concise, if useless, notation for a number of properties. Items below use notation for morphisms of finite topological spaces defined in the page on
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/separation+axioms+in+terms+of+lifting+properties"} separation axioms in terms of lifting properties
          %h4#uniform_spaces Uniform spaces
          %p
            In the category of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/uniform+spaces"} uniform spaces
            or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+spaces"} metric spaces
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/uniformly+continuous"} uniformly continuous
            maps.
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                A space
